Bash(git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
fix(#66): let sandcastle's browser verify local pages without base64

playwright-mcp blocks file:// navigation by default (allowUnrestrictedFileAccess
is false), so an agent trying to preview a rendered local page had to
base64-encode it into a data: URL instead — expensive, and unnecessary since
data: URLs reach the same host Chrome over the same CDP connection anyway.
Pass --allow-unrestricted-file-access on the sandbox's own playwright-mcp
connect script (never on any host-side MCP config) to unblock it, with a
comment on the real trade-off: the browser on the other end of that CDP
connection is a real host Chrome process, so this grants read access to the
host filesystem, not just this disposable container — confirmed directly by
navigating to file:///Users/ during verification and getting back a real
directory listing.

Also fixes the efficiency-rules.md instruction that told agents to fall back
to curl "only if the MCP tools are genuinely unavailable": the recorded run
this rule was meant to help had the tools available, they just couldn't
reach the target — read literally, the rule forbade the fallback it was
supposed to prescribe. Now keyed on page reachability, and collapsed from a
9-sentence paragraph to two lines.

Verified in-session: browser_navigate to file:///, file:///Users/, and
file:///Users/magnus.volkmann/ all rendered directory listings with no
protocol error, before and after confirming the flag change took effect by
killing and letting the MCP harness respawn the playwright-mcp server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
)"
